    {
      "tagline": "Submit a 311 request about an animal nuisance violation.",
      "why": "Report common animal nuisance offenses involving a cat, dog, livestock, or wildlife, including failure to clean up animal waste, too many animals in a living space, a barking dog, spay/neuter or vaccination violations, unsanitary conditions, microchip issues, and tethering violations. The 311 request form asks whether the animal is owned, where it lives, what violation occurred, and whether the property is gated. For a barking dog it asks when barking typically occurs and requires the complainant’s and violator’s names and addresses for follow-up.",
      "why_not": "A barking-dog complaint without the complainant’s name and address and the violator’s name and address will not be responded to, according to the 311 request form.",
      "what": "Submit 311 request",
      "who": "Dallas Animal Services",
      "how": "Go to Dallas 311 > Choose \"Animal Care and Control\" > Choose \"Animal Nuisance\"",
